Package: linuwu-sense-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Recommends:
 linux-headers-amd64 | linux-headers-generic | linux-headers,
 mokutil,
Conflicts: linuwu-sense
Replaces: linuwu-sense
Provides: linuwu-sense-kernel
Description: WMI driver for Acer Predator and Nitro laptops (DKMS source)
 linuwu_sense replaces the in-kernel acer_wmi driver and adds what the kernel
 version does not expose on Acer gaming laptops: fan control, thermal profiles
 with Turbo mode, an 80% battery charge limiter, battery calibration,
 four-zone RGB keyboard backlight, LCD override, and USB charging while the
 machine is off.
 .
 The module is built on your own machine through DKMS, so it is rebuilt
 automatically on every kernel upgrade.
 .
 This is a fork of Div-Linuwu-Sense that adds compatibility with the
 platform_profile API of kernels older than 6.13 (such as the 6.12 LTS in
 Debian 13), completes the Predator PH315-53 quirk, and fixes four-zone RGB so
 that per-zone colours actually light up.
 .
 You do not normally install this package by hand: acer-powersave depends on
 it.

Package: acer-powersave
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
 python3-gi,
 gir1.2-glib-2.0,
 power-profiles-daemon,
 linuwu-sense-dkms (= ${binary:Version}),
Recommends:
 libkf6screen-bin | kscreen,
Suggests:
 powertop,
Conflicts: tlp, auto-cpufreq, tuned
Description: hardware and power management for Acer Predator and Nitro laptops
 Everything that talks to the hardware: power profiles, keyboard backlight,
 fans, battery and the discrete GPU. It pulls in the linuwu_sense kernel
 driver, so this one package is enough for a working machine without any
 graphical interface. Install acer-sense on top if you want one.
 .
 Power profiles follow power-profiles-daemon and keep no state of their own on
 disk: the active PPD profile is the single source of truth. Under KDE,
 PowerDevil already maps AC and battery to a profile, so this follows the
 mains cable and still honours a manual override.
 .
 Includes:
  * CPU governor, EPP and turbo per profile, undoing the fixed frequency cap
    PPD applies in power-saver (measured on a PH315-53, that cap costs 3.3x
    more energy for the same work);
  * panel refresh rate per profile through a session service, which Plasma
    does not offer (PowerDevil does not manage display configuration);
  * hot plug and unplug of the NVIDIA Optimus GPU, with no reboot and without
    needing envycontrol;
  * keyboard backlight brightness on the Fn keys, corrected so the bottom of
    the range switches the light off instead of jumping back to maximum;
  * fan curve with hysteresis;
  * idle power measurement that discards samples taken under load.
 .
 It does not touch screen brightness.

Package: acer-sense
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
 python3-pyqt6,
 acer-powersave (= ${binary:Version}),
Description: graphical control panel for Acer Predator and Nitro laptops
 A PredatorSense-like interface built on the linuwu_sense driver and on
 power-profiles-daemon. It needs acer-powersave, which provides the hardware
 layer and the kernel driver.
 .
 Includes:
  * live monitoring of temperatures, fan speed, power draw and CPU state;
  * fan control: automatic, manual, or an editable curve where you set the
    temperature at which the fans start and how steeply they ramp up;
  * keyboard backlight: effects, speed, direction, brightness, and a fixed
    colour per zone on four-zone keyboards;
  * power profiles, panel refresh rate, and hot plug of the NVIDIA GPU;
  * battery charge limit, calibration and firmware settings.
 .
 It opens with the laptop's dedicated key (PredatorSense on Predator models,
 the N key on Nitro), which this package sets up for you.
